<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea to allow foreigners OTC trading in 1997.</title>
<headline>S.Korea to allow foreigners OTC trading in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea would allow foreigners direct access to the over-the-counter stock market sometime during the first half of 1997, the domestic Yonhap news agency said on Sunday.</p>
<p>Quoting an official at the finance ministry, Yonhap said the combined foreign shareholding would be limited at 10 percent of a stock and individual investment would not exceed three percent.</p>
<p>Currently, foreigners can only invest through institutionally managed funds.</p>
<p>Officials at the ministry were not available for comment.</p>
</text>
